5.2
SFR-Judges produce factual critiques.
Thus far, we have focused on evaluating the cor-
rectness of the final judgement. However, while
the final judgement may be consistent with the
ground-truth, the critique itself may be inconsistent
or hallucinated. We therefore use the MetaCritique
framework (Sun et al., 2024), which uses GPT-4
to evaluate critique quality via atomic information
units (AIUs), i,e., simple true/false statements. An-
swers to these AIUs are used to compute Meta-
Precision (measure of factuality) and Meta-Recall
(measure of completeness with respect to a GPT-4
generated critique), which are aggregated into a
Meta-F1 score (measure of overall critique qual-
ity). We evaluate our models, Themis, and Self-
taught-evaluator and report performance in Table 4.
We additionally report the performance of Auto-
J (Li et al., 2023a), UltraCM (Cui et al., 2023),
SelFee (Ye et al., 2023a), and human criti

