5.3
Incorporating a New LLM into an
Existing Leaderboard
While our main focus has been on ranking multi-
ple LLMs at once, it is also useful to consider the
common scenario of adding a single new model to
an existing leaderboard, which is also frequent use-
case. We explored two approaches: (1) a binary
search-like placement method, and (2) using the
top-performing model response as a baseline. Our
findings indicate that the later approach is more
reliable (Table 5, Appendix). Further details and
discussions are provided in Appendix A.6.


