Due to the ordinal and discrete nature of ratings, a
continuous interval whose upper and lower bounds
are continuous numeric values might not have ex-
act meaning. Thus, we further apply a boundary
adjustment strategy to transform the continuous in-
terval to an ordinal interval whose upper and lower
bounds align with the potential rating labels.
Specifically, boundary adjustment is essentially
redefining the non-conformity score function as
