4.2
Continuous Intervals Indicate Uncertainty
Table 1 presents the interval width and coverage
rate for each conformal prediction methods on Sum-
mEval evaluated by G-Eval and on ROSCOE eval-
uted SocREval. Additional results on DialSumm
are presented in Table 12. From these results, most
conformal predictors consistently output prediction
intervals with coverage close to the 90% in sum-
marization tasks, indicating that LLM judges are
confident when evaluating summarization tasks, es-
pecially on fluency. However, most methods fail
to achieve 90% (or close to 90%) coverage rate in
reasoning tasks, and the interval widths are high in
a few cases where 90% coverage is achieved. One
possible reason is that ROSCOE has much fewer
samples, resulting in poor calibration.
4.3
All Coverages Improve after Adjustment
