4.4
Coverage and label-space effects
Empirical coverage lies within one percentage
point of the 90% target on every dataset, demon-
strating that a single conformal wrapper gener-
alises from an 11-point rubric (ASAP) to 3-labeled
(TOEFL11, FCE) despite the shift in prompt style,
score range and proficiency level. The larger pre-
diction sets observed on ASAP reflect the richer
label space: with eleven possible scores the model
must sometimes hedge between adja

